Program– 02: SortingScores in DescendingOrder (BubbleSort)
OR sort race score(descending)

Algorithm:
Step 1: [Start]
Step 2: Inputnumberof students n.
Step 3: Inputn scores into array scores[].
Step 4: For i =0ton-2:
    o Forj=0ton-i-2:
        If scores[j] < scores[j+1], swap them.
Step 5: Printsorted scores in descending order.
Step 6: [Stop]

CSource Code:
#include <stdio.h>
#include <conio.h>
int main()
{
    int n, i, j, temp;
    int scores[100];
    clrscr();
    printf("Enter number of students: ");
    scanf("%d", &n);
    printf("Enter the scores:\n");
    for(i = 0; i < n; i++)
        scanf("%d", &scores[i]);
    // Bubble Sort(Descending Order)
    for(i = 0; i < n-1; i++)
    {
        for(j = 0; j < n-i-1; j++)
        {
            if(scores[j] < scores[j+1])
            {
                temp = scores[j];
                scores[j] = scores[j+1];
                scores[j+1] = temp;
            }
        }
    }
    printf("Scores in descending order:\n");
    for(i = 0; i < n; i++)
        printf("%d ", scores[i]);
    getch();
    return 0;
}
